{
  "_note": "Snapshot of the orin-dev-kit (Jetson AGX Orin, Ubuntu 24.04, JetPack 7, viam-server 1.13) machine config, 2026-10-23. SO-101 leader + follower with teleop (auto_start on). Both calibration sensors are disabled (only needed to recalibrate). Cameras: arm-camera and webcam-2 (the wrist camera; its frame is an estimate, to be verified), detections-view (YOLOv8s detections drawn on webcam-2), and webcam-2-depth / webcam-2-range: Depth Anything 3 metric depth, a point cloud and lidar-style ranges from webcam-2, served by the local module in modules/depth-anything-3 (installed at /home/ultraviolet/depth-anything-3 on the Orin; preview page on 127.0.0.1:8766). spoon = collision box for the spoon taped in the fixed jaw (on follower-gripper, whose frame is the jaw-tip TCP), so the motion planner keeps it off the table. The ViamShellDanger shell service comes from a fragment, not listed here. No secrets are stored here.",
